{%- comment -%}
  Edition I — the homepage's signature "entering an Edition" moment, not a text-left/image-right
  teaser. One pinned cinematic composition, four scroll states, released directly into Object in
  focus. CAVIERA is Edition-based, not a permanent catalogue — no product grid, no prices, no Add
  to Bag, no /collections/all. Informational by design while Edition I has no dedicated page yet —
  cta_text/cta_url are both blank by default; the section reads as complete with no action at all.

  FOUR SCROLL STATES (see the --edition-* custom properties in caviera-home.css, all derived from
  the one --caviera-progress value assets/caviera-scroll-progress.js already writes onto this
  [data-caviera-pin] section — no second scroll engine):
    01 ARRIVAL     (progress 0.00–0.20)  calm resting composition, nothing moving yet.
    02 APPROACHES  (progress 0.20–0.45)  media 01 tightens toward a closer crop (scale up to
                                          ~1.14, object-position drifting toward the object).
    03 ENTERS      (progress 0.45–0.72)  media 02 recomposes into the frame beside media 01 — an
                                          editorial choreography (Toasted Buns, translated), not a
                                          static crossfade.
    04 RESOLUTION  (progress 0.72–1.00)  media 02 grows toward dominance, media 01 partially
                                          retreats, metadata stays anchored, then the section
                                          releases into Object in focus.
  EDITION I itself drifts a further few vw horizontally throughout (Drkst), continuously, not in
  discrete steps.

  Media architecture ("Edition media 01/02/03" in the Theme Editor — edition_image_1/2/3 as
  settings IDs, unchanged, to preserve any values already saved): media 01 is the primary image,
  falling back to the same bundled default the hero uses (assets/15_oryx_necklace_on_model.png,
  the only jewellery/object photograph bundled with this theme) when unset. media 02/03 are each
  either a merchant's own dedicated image OR — when left blank — media 01 reused with a strongly
  differentiated crop/scale/object-position (see [data-derived="true"] in caviera-home.css), so
  there are always genuinely different-looking states even with only one real asset available, and
  the same photo never visibly repeats identically. media 03 is a small optional detail inset only
  (kept deliberately minor per the "no more than ~3 visual frames, 2 most of the time" brief).

  Below 900px, under prefers-reduced-motion, or if the script never runs: no pin, no sticky, no
  scroll-driven transforms at all — a complete static composition (title, metadata, copy, media 01,
  media 02) in plain document flow. See the var(--caviera-progress, 0) fallback on every consumer
  in caviera-home.css.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img1 = section.settings.edition_image_1
  assign img2 = section.settings.edition_image_2
  assign img3 = section.settings.edition_image_3
  assign bundled_file = '15_oryx_necklace_on_model.png'
  assign use_bundled = false
  if img1 == blank
    assign use_bundled = true
  endif
  assign has_meta = false
  if section.settings.edition_number != blank or section.settings.edition_status != blank
    assign has_meta = true
  endif
  assign edition_num = section.settings.edition_number | default: '01'
  assign token_text = 'No. ' | append: edition_num

  # media 02/03: a merchant's own dedicated image always wins; otherwise both reuse media 01 (or
  # the bundled default) so there are always genuine second/third states, never one that simply
  # never renders.
  assign img2_derived = false
  assign img2_render = img2
  if img2 == blank
    assign img2_derived = true
    assign img2_render = img1
  endif
  assign img3_derived = false
  assign img3_render = img3
  if img3 == blank
    assign img3_derived = true
    assign img3_render = img1
  endif
-%}
<section id="edition-i" class="caviera-section caviera-edition-teaser" data-scheme="{{ section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'obsidian' }}" data-caviera-pin>
  <div class="container caviera-edition-teaser__inner">
    <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__copy" data-reveal>
      {%- if has_meta -%}
        <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__meta label" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- section.settings.edition_number -}}
          {%- if section.settings.edition_number != blank and section.settings.edition_status != blank %} / {% endif -%}
          {{- section.settings.edition_status -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Drkst-style typographic moment: this heading (nested [data-reveal] of its own, independent
          of the copy block's outer reveal above) enters oversized and settles — see [data-reveal-
          style="drkst"] in caviera-motion.css — AND, being inside the [data-caviera-pin] wrapper
          above, continues drifting horizontally in step with --caviera-progress for as long as the
          section stays pinned (see .caviera-edition-teaser__heading.is-visible in caviera-motion.
          css) — a visible, continuous, architectural movement, never split into letters, never
          rotated. Opt-out via heading_motion below; the plain static heading renders with no code
          change either way.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h2
          class="caviera-edition-teaser__heading"
          {%- if section.settings.heading_motion %} data-reveal data-reveal-style="drkst"{% endif %}
        >
          {{ section.settings.heading }}
          {%- if section.settings.year_label != blank -%}
            <span class="caviera-edition-teaser__year">{{ section.settings.year_label }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <p class="body-text caviera-edition-teaser__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.structure_line != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Optional, restrained — the planned Edition structure ("10–12 creations"), never framed as
          current inventory or urgency. Blank by default; prefer leaving it blank if the composition
          reads stronger without it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="caviera-edition-teaser__structure label">{{ section.settings.structure_line }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.cta_text != blank and section.settings.cta_url != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url }}" class="link-underline caviera-edition-teaser__cta">{{ section.settings.cta_text }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media"{% if section.settings.show_token %} data-caviera-drag-zone{% endif %}>
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media-primary" data-reveal data-reveal-style="crop">
        {%- if img1 != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ img1 | image_url: width: 1000 }}"
            srcset="{{ img1 | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ img1 | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w, {{ img1 | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w"
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 84vw"
            width="{{ img1.width }}"
            height="{{ img1.height }}"
            alt="{{ img1.alt | default: section.settings.heading | default: 'Edition I' | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif use_bundled -%}
          <img
            src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}"
            width="521" height="358"
            alt="{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Edition I' | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        STATE 03/04 — always renders (a real merchant image if provided, otherwise media 01 reused
        with a strongly differentiated "centre macro" crop — see [data-derived="true"] in caviera-
        home.css) so the choreographed second visual never depends on photography that doesn't
        exist yet. Recomposes into the frame beside media 01 rather than simply crossfading in place.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media-secondary" data-derived="{{ img2_derived }}" data-reveal data-reveal-style="mask" style="transition-delay: 140ms;">
        {%- if img2_render != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ img2_render | image_url: width: 700 }}"
            srcset="{{ img2_render | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ img2_render | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ img2_render | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w"
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 28vw, 56vw"
            width="{{ img2_render.width }}"
            height="{{ img2_render.height }}"
            alt="{{ img2_render.alt | default: 'Edition I — detail' | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif use_bundled -%}
          <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="Edition I — detail" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        STATE 04 only — a small, minor detail inset (never more than ~3 frames total, per brief).
        Same always-renders principle: a real merchant detail image if provided, otherwise media 01
        reused a third time with a third, differently-centred crop.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="caviera-edition-teaser__media-detail" data-derived="{{ img3_derived }}">
        {%- if img3_render != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ img3_render | image_url: width: 500 }}"
            srcset="{{ img3_render | image_url: width: 300 }} 300w, {{ img3_render | image_url: width: 500 }} 500w, {{ img3_render | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w"
            sizes="(min-width: 900px) 16vw, 40vw"
            width="{{ img3_render.width }}"
            height="{{ img3_render.height }}"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- elsif use_bundled -%}
          <img src="{{ bundled_file | asset_url }}" width="521" height="358" alt="" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Bureau Nine's Edition/spatial-progression idea — a single small, bounded, draggable Edition
        plaque token (rectangular archival plaque, not the hero's circular medallion), floating over
        the composition. This section stays primarily scroll choreography, not a second draggable
        playground — see the hero for the full three-artifact interaction. Desktop pointer only;
        fully visible and static everywhere else, per assets/caviera-drag-token.js (unchanged).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_token -%}
        {%- render 'caviera-drag-token', type: 'number', text: token_text, mode: 'dark', cue: 'Move' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Edition I teaser",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour", "default": "obsidian",
      "info": "Obsidian is the intended default — night/theatre/anticipation, distinct from the hero's warmer Cinnabar energy.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "obsidian", "label": "Obsidian" },
        { "value": "cinnabar", "label": "Cinnabar" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "edition_number", "label": "Number", "default": "01" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "edition_status", "label": "Status", "default": "Upcoming", "info": "Quiet metadata, not a sale badge — avoid hype language (\"Limited drop\", \"Only X left\", \"Coming soon!!!\")." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "EDITION I" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "heading_motion", "label": "Architectural heading movement", "default": true, "info": "The heading enters slightly oversized and settles, then drifts horizontally in step with scroll while the section stays pinned. Off falls back to the plain static heading with no motion at all." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "year_label", "label": "Year", "default": "2026" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Supporting line", "default": "The first CAVIERA Edition is in preparation." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "structure_line", "label": "Structure line (optional)", "info": "e.g. \"10–12 creations\" — only if clearly framed as the planned Edition structure, never current inventory. Leave blank if the composition is stronger without it. Avoid \"Limited drop\"/\"Exclusive\"/\"Only X available\"." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Action text (optional)", "info": "Leave blank to keep the section purely informational — appropriate while Edition I has no dedicated page yet. Avoid \"Add to Bag\"/\"Shop Edition\"/\"Buy Now\"." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_url", "label": "Action link (optional)", "info": "Only shown when Action text above is also set. Never point this at /collections/all." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Images" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Up to three visual states in the scroll sequence. Any left blank temporarily reuse Edition media 01 (or the bundled default) with a distinct crop, rather than never appearing — replace with real Edition campaign photography here at any time, no code change required." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "edition_image_1", "label": "Edition media 01 (primary)", "info": "Gender-neutral jewellery/object imagery preferred — this House is for both men and women. Falls back to a bundled default when left blank." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "edition_image_2", "label": "Edition media 02 (optional)", "info": "The second state the composition recomposes around. Falls back to a strongly differentiated crop of media 01 when left blank." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "edition_image_3", "label": "Edition media 03 (optional)", "info": "A small detail inset only, arriving last. Falls back to a third, differently cropped treatment of media 01 when left blank." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Interaction" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_token", "label": "Show draggable Edition plaque token", "default": true, "info": "A single small, bounded, draggable Edition-number token floating over the composition — desktop pointer input only. Stays static and fully visible on touch, keyboard-only, and reduced-motion visits." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Edition I teaser" }],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["index"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
